# Change Note — 26 September 2026

Three changes shipped today. Two were bug fixes to the data layer; one changes what the
strategy is allowed to buy. All three were tested before shipping.

---

## 1. Bug 3 — phantom trading sessions · FIXED

**Symptom.** The panel contained roughly 60 sessions on which nothing actually traded. Republic Day
2023, Holi 2023 and Independence Day 2024 all carried full rows, with 99.9% of closes identical to
the prior day.

**Root cause.** `build_artifacts.py` took the session date from the FILENAME:

```python
sub["date"] = ds[4:] + ds[2:4] + ds[:2]     # DDMMYYYY -> YYYYMMDD
```

NSE serves the PREVIOUS session's file when you request a market-holiday URL, so real data was
stamped with a date on which the market was shut.

**Fix.** Read `DATE1` from inside the file and reject any row whose internal date disagrees with the
filename. Plus `drop_duplicates` on (date, symbol) as a backstop. Rejected files are written to
`artifacts/phantom_sessions.csv` and raise a manifest warning.

**Result.**

| | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| Panel sessions | 1,483 | **1,414** |
| Files rejected | — | **70** |
| Remaining duplicate-session pairs | ~60 | **0** |
| Weekday gaps across 5.7 years | 12 | **82** |

82 gaps is correct — NSE takes 13-16 holidays a year. Per year: 14, 13, 15, 16, 13, 11.

**Why it mattered.** Flat sessions depress ATR and realised volatility and shift every rolling
window, so stops and position sizes were computed on softened inputs.

